# 🚩 Challenge: [ASCII FTW]
![alt text](asciiftw.png)
## 📝 Challenge Description
This program has constructed the flag using hex ascii values. Identify the flag text by disassembling the program. You can download the file from here
.

Hints
1. The combined range of hex-ascii for English alphabets and numerical digits is from 30 to 7A.

2. Online hex-ascii converters can be helpful.


### Code / Terminal Snippets
```bash
1. wget https://challenge-files.cylabacademy.net/library/1f9ccb30f15b0d3c8f20388a8e187101cfc688bb04ca9437e4ad695920f91f64/asciiftw
2. gdb asciiftw
3. disassemble main
4. break *main+202
5. run
6. x/s $rbp-0x30
```

---

## 🚀 Exploitation / Solution Path
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. Download the challenge file using `wget`.
2. Debug the file code with `gdb` and `disassemble` the code with main.
3. Set a breakpoint to the program with main and run and examine based on string from starting point `0x30`.
4. The flag will be displayed.
---

